SECURITY ISSUE F: AUTHORIZATION

Every protected endpoint must verify authorization independently.

Never rely only on hidden navigation items or frontend role checks.

Enforce project membership and resource ownership at the backend.

Create and verify a centralized authorization layer.

The authorization rules must account for:

PI_LEAD:
- Authorized project administration.
- Team management.
- Review and publishing permissions as defined by the product.
- Restricted PI-only content.
- Sensitive-data reveal only through the appropriate authenticated process.

RESEARCHER:
- Authorized shared-source ingestion.
- Authorized record and note editing.
- Reconstruction and permitted workflow operations.
- No privileged administration.
- No unauthorized restricted-source access.

REVIEWER:
- Authorized evidence inspection.
- Review decisions.
- No unauthorized project administration.
- No handover publishing unless separately authorized.

INCOMING_MEMBER:
- Published and authorized handover only.
- Permitted acknowledgement.
- Cold-Start questions based on the authorized published handover.
- No access to restricted source material, private drafts or other members' private evaluation answers.

AUDITOR:
- Read-only audit access according to project permissions.
- No unauthorized editing or publishing.

Never assume that a role alone grants access to every project.

SECURITY ISSUE G: PRIVATE AND RESTRICTED CONTENT

Implement the following strict rules:

PRIVATE_OWNER:
- Only the authenticated owner may access the private source or note.
- Other users, including PI_LEAD, must not receive the private content unless an explicit, documented product permission is introduced.
- Private sources must not be included in shared reconstruction.
- Private sources must not appear in shared handovers.
- Private sources must not leak through error messages, search results, counts, logs or metadata.
- Owner-only access must be checked server-side.

RESTRICTED_PI_ONLY:
- Only authorized PI_LEAD users may access restricted content.
- Other roles must not retrieve the original content through any API.
- Ensure restrictions apply to spans, downloads, previews, summaries, search, notes and handovers.

PROJECT_SHARED:
- Available only to authorized members of that project.

Create automated cross-role and cross-project isolation tests.

SECURITY ISSUE H: FILE UPLOADS

Review every upload route.

Implement:

- Strict extension allowlist.
- MIME verification.
- File signature validation where possible.
- Maximum file size.
- Safe filenames.
- Random server-generated storage names.
- Path traversal prevention.
- Duplicate detection.
- Atomic writes.
- Temporary file cleanup after failure.
- No direct public storage access.
- No executable uploads.
- No unsafe HTML rendering.
- Correct cleanup after deletion.
- Correct source ownership and visibility checks.

Retain support for the existing PDF, Markdown, text, CSV and JSON formats.

Image-only PDFs must be marked NEEDS_OCR. Never pretend OCR succeeded if it did not.

SECURITY ISSUE I: SECRETS AND DATA PROTECTION

- Keep Gemini API keys exclusively on the server.
- Never expose environment variables to the browser.
- Never commit .env files.
- Provide a complete .env.example without real credentials.
